From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] shell32: SHStartNetConnectionDialogW, SHOpenPropSheetW/A, SHInvokePrinterCommandW/A

Spec stubs, and SHStartNetConnectionDialogW and SHOpenPropSheetW were not exported by name (Shell32.lib names
them), so a program importing them did not start; a caller of the others crashed. As Microsoft documents them:
- SHStartNetConnectionDialogW (14) / A (12): Map Network Drive with the remote name given, always S_OK;
  mpr's dialog now honours CONNDLG_RO_PATH (the folder box read-only).
- SHOpenPropSheetW (80) / A (707): the default CLSID's pages and the PropertySheetHandlers of each key, the
  handlers initialized with the data object and the key, modal, at the named start page; no pages is FALSE.
  SHCreatePropSheetExtArrayEx closed its caller's key when given no subkey (RegOpenKey hands back the same
  handle). comctl32: PSH_USEPSTARTPAGE starts at the page pStartPage names (it always started at the first).
- SHInvokePrinterCommandW/A: properties, printing preferences (the person's defaults, SetPrinter level 9), a
  test page, network printer connection, a shortcut to a printer; open goes to Settings' printers page (no
  separate queue window); server properties ERROR_NOT_SUPPORTED. A shortcut to a printer kept no target when
  loaded (pcheck did not know printer pidls).
Gates: test/netdlg-gate.sh, test/propsheet-gate.sh, test/printcmd-gate.sh.
---
